    L003 is independent of the A001/A002 arithmetic branch and the
    M001/L001/L002 regulator-metatheory branch.


6 - File Guide
    ----------

    L003_00_Premises.v

      Shared relational vocabulary and abstract hypotheses. Defines `Tot2`,
      `EvalC`, `CompilerCorrect`, and `EvaluatorDiagonalClosure`.

    L003_01__Binary_Evaluation.v

      Constructive consequences of exact binary totality: output uniqueness,
      binary exhaustion, and the complementary `0`/`1` equivalences.

    L003_02__Evaluator_Relative_Nonclosure.v

      Primary abstract theorems. Proves evaluator-relative exclusion,
      pointwise exclusion on diagonally closed domains, and nonexistence of a
      total evaluator correct on such a domain.

    L003_03__Compiled_Countermachine.v

      Internal even/odd code layout and inductively generated compiled output
      relation. Proves code separation, diagonal behavior, concrete compiler
      correctness, and the specialized nonclosure theorem.

    L003_04__Indexed_Judgment.v

      Minimal assigned-label/active-label separation. Provides the checking
      countermodel, witnessed-binding lemmas, and bound-evaluator nonclosure.

    L003_95_API.v

      Stable package API. Re-exports both development branches and names the
      six public contracts together with `L003_CORE_CONTRACT`.

    L003_97_Artifacts.v

      Certifies each named contract, proves `l003_core_qed`, and redirects six
      `Print Assumptions` reports.

    _appendix/_assumptions/

      Generated assumption reports for the primary abstract, indexed-self,
      concrete, and aggregate endpoints. All six reports are closed under the
      global context.


7 - Public API
    ----------

    The stable downstream import is:

      `From L003 Require Import L003_95_API.`

    Abstract vocabulary:

      Code, Input, Output                                              (00)
      OutputRelation, HaltingRelation, QueryCoding                     (00)
      DiagonalCompiler, BinaryOutput, Tot2                             (00)
      EvalC, CompilerCorrect, EvaluatorDiagonalClosure                 (00)

    Abstract headline theorems:

      evaluator_relative_nonclosure                                   (02)
      diagonally_closed_domain_excludes_evaluator                     (02)
      no_total_evaluator_on_diagonally_closed_domain                  (02)

    Concrete compiled semantics:

      base_machine_code, compiled_diagonal_code                       (03)
      CompiledOutput, CompiledHalt                                    (03)
      compiled_countermachine_correct                                 (03)
      concrete_evaluator_relative_nonclosure                          (03)

    Indexed-label surface:

      IndexedSelfConfiguration, SelfTokenChecks, SelfTokenBound       (04)
      WitnessedSelfJudgment, BoundEvaluator                           (04)
      indexed_self_checking_does_not_supply_binding                   (04)
      bound_evaluator_relative_nonclosure                             (04)

    Contract surface:

      EVALUATOR_RELATIVE_NONCLOSURE_CONTRACT                          (95)
      DIAGONALLY_CLOSED_DOMAIN_EXCLUSION_CONTRACT                     (95)
      INDEXED_SELF_CHECKING_NONENTAILMENT_CONTRACT                    (95)
      BOUND_EVALUATOR_NONCLOSURE_CONTRACT                             (95)
      CONCRETE_COMPILER_CORRECTNESS_CONTRACT                          (95)
      CONCRETE_EVALUATOR_NONCLOSURE_CONTRACT                          (95)
      L003_CORE_CONTRACT                                              (95)

    Aggregate certified endpoint:

      l003_core_qed : L003_CORE_CONTRACT                              (97)


8 - Notes
    -----

    `L003_03__Compiled_Countermachine` and
    `L003_04__Indexed_Judgment` are independent branches after the abstract
    theorem layer; `L003_95_API` deliberately joins them.

    The artifact file writes assumption reports and should not be used as a
    routine downstream import. Import `L003_95_API` for the stable theorem and
    contract surface.

    The package has no extraction or IO layer. Its artifacts are proof
    endpoints and assumption reports only.
